,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.797222643,"data":"WHAT MAY AND MAY NOT BE READ OFF THIS\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.797968358,"data":"  * All five rungs produced the hand-written side's own bytes on this card,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.798740617,"data":"    on the state the hand-written side produced, before any of them was\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.799526619,"data":"    timed, and all five trace the same rays (mean DDA steps above).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.800291681,"data":"  * Every rung is the rung above plus exactly one rewrite, so the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.801102712,"data":"    difference between consecutive rows is that rewrite's price.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.801880992,"data":"  * The reference denominator is measured HERE, on THIS card, in THIS\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.802729507,"data":"    session. It is not a number copied out of another run.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.803587721,"data":"  * COLD vs WARM: only the first graph built at a shape goes through\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.804390286,"data":"    Allocator.alloc, so only a cold graph has an allocator peak, and only a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.805091226,"data":"    cold graph has the schedule that goes with a cold allocator. Both are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.805844795,"data":"    reported. The times do not depend on which it is.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3114.80667895,"data":"  * No number in this file is transcribed from a notes file.\n"}
